            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="LAN05" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName/>
                        <forename>John Henry</forename>
                        <surname>Petty</surname>
                        <addName>marquess of Lansdowne</addName>
                    </persName>
                    <birth notBefore="1764" notAfter="1764">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1809-11-14"/>
                    <occupation>politician</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Lansdowne held the title of Marquess of Lansdowne for only four years. He succeeded his father the first <persName key="LAN04">Marquess of Lansdowne</persName> 
      in 1805 and was in turn succeeded by
       his half-brother, <persName key="LAN06">Henry Petty Fitzmaurice</persName>. The <title>DNB</title> states that he led an eccentric life and suffered from ill-health.</p>
                        <p>His dates of birth and death can be deduced from funeral notices and obituaries in <title>The Times</title>, 24 November 1809, the <title>Morning Chronicle</title>, 
    19 November 1809, and <title>Aberdeen Journal</title>, 22 November 1809. </p>
                        <p>Godwin records his death.</p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="other">
